      "question": "If $\\sqrt[3]{a/b} = \\dfrac{5}{6}$, find $a/b$ and $a + b$.",
      "answer": "$a/b = \\dfrac{125}{216}$; $a + b = 341$",
      "options": [],
      "glassboxSteps": [
        {
          "rule": "Cube both sides",
          "why": "Reverse the cube root.",
          "math": "\\dfrac{a}{b} = \\left(\\dfrac{5}{6}\\right)^3 = \\dfrac{125}{216}"
        },
        {
          "rule": "Sum",
          "why": "If $a=125$, $b=216$ in simplest form.",
          "math": "a + b = 125 + 216 = 341"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "$a/b = \\frac{125}{216}$; $a+b = 341$.",
      "linked_note_id": "CH04-sec-cubes-and-cube-roots",
      "source": "practice-session"
